# tool-inventory: one line per tool, read by tool-check (daily on the Mac Mini).
#
#   name | check command     exit 0 = healthy (run by sh, PATH includes ~/scripts and Homebrew)
#   name | syntax            parse-only check (zsh -n, bash -n, sh -n, python ast), chosen by shebang
#   name | [300s] command    optional timeout, default 60s; a hang counts as broken
#   name | skip: reason      deliberately not exercised
#
# A new executable at the top of ~/scripts or in ~/tools/<tool>/ needs a line here, or tool-check
# reports it as "not inventoried". Pick the smallest side-effect-free proof the tool starts:
# --help, --version, a read-only list. Read the tool's source first: some treat unknown args as
# input (send-to-claude would send "--help" as a message). If unsure, use syntax or skip.
# ~/tools/*/test.sh and tests/run-all.sh run automatically; hooks/ is covered by run-all.sh.

# --- ~/scripts: real start-up checks
agent-audio | agent-audio status
